{{!-- v3 "Personaje" tab — bio (identity) + Features, merged (add-pc-sheet-v3 §8.1/§8.2).

      WHY THIS MERGE, RE-DERIVED ACROSS ALL 13 SPLATS (design.md D9)
      ----------------------------------------------------------------
      Only FOUR splats declare bio splatfields at all (vampire 6, werewolf 5, mage 7, wraith 7);
      `mortal` declares `{}` and eight declare nothing. So for nine of thirteen splats the standalone
      Bio tab was a portrait, a name, four generic fields and two prose boxes — the tab that should
      not exist alone. Merging it into the Features tab (renamed "Personaje", `wod.tab.character`)
      gives those nine a tab with something in it, and the four that do declare fields simply get a
      richer one. The `bio` PARTS/tab entry is retired once this renders verified (§8.1's own
      instruction); see `pc-actor-sheet-v3.js` for the retirement.

      HOW THE CONTEXT GOT HERE. `prepareFeatureContext` now calls `addBioContext` (§8.1), the exact
      body `prepareBioContext` always ran, extracted so both callers share it byte-for-byte — the
      `applyDeclaredSplatfieldTypes` -> `backfillDeclaredSplatfields` order is load-bearing and lives
      entirely inside that shared function, so nothing here can disturb it. Every key this section
      reads (`appearance`, `splatfields`, `listData`, `enrichedAppearance`, …) is therefore identical
      to what `templates/actor/v3/bio.hbs` read, and that file's markup is reproduced verbatim below
      — same partials, same arguments, same order, same three documented compromises (disclosure-not-
      clamp on long splatfield prose, no persisted unfold state, textboxes only). Read
      `templates/actor/v3/bio.hbs`'s own header (kept on disk until the `bio` part retires) for the
      full reasoning; it is not repeated here a second time.

      THE ITEM LISTS BELOW (§8.5 — render once, not twice)
      ------------------------------------------------------
      Backgrounds, Merits, Flaws and Other Traits used to print HERE as well as on the Stats tab
      (`stats_features.hbs`), from the one `prepareAdvantageLists` call — a genuine render duplicate,
      not a data one. MEASURED before choosing which copy to keep: the Stats tab's row
      (`stats_feature_row.hbs`) is the ONLY place on either sheet that lets a player EDIT a
      Background's or Other Trait's rating — it renders an editable dot row
      (`stat_value_dots.hbs` -> `OnDotCounterChange`, writing `system.value` on the item); this tab's
      row (`feature_item.hbs`) has never rendered anything but a read-only number for these four
      kinds. Removing the Stats copy would have deleted the ONLY way to change a Background's dots
      anywhere on the sheet — the exact "lose no affordance" failure this change is written against.
      So the STATS TAB keeps them (`v3/stats.hbs` is unchanged), and this tab stops re-drawing them.
      What THIS tab's copy had that Stats' does not — drag-reorder, the activation toggle and
      send-to-chat (`feature_item.hbs` via `list_icons.hbs`) — is ported onto `stats_feature_row.hbs`
      instead, so nothing this tab used to offer is lost either; see that partial's own comments for
      what changed and why porting there (a single-caller partial) carries far less fork risk than
      retrofitting an editable dot column into `feature_item.hbs`, which twelve other blocks share.
      Bloodbound / Boon / Oath / Passion / Dark Passion / Fetter / the connection roster / Other
      Traits' SHADOW-area exception are untouched — none of those render on the Stats tab, so there
      is nothing to dedupe for them.

      Everything else in the "FIFTH PART MIGRATED" section below — the shell/row split, the
      Experience ledgers' DOM contract, what is deliberately not "fixed" — is unchanged from the
      original Features-only version of this file and is not restated a second time. --}}
<section class="tab {{tab.cssClass}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}" data-drop-area="true">

	<div class="v3-tabhead">
		<h2 class="v3-tabtitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.tab.character"}}</h2>

		{{!-- Same two v2 defects as every other tab's create control: a 3x-scaled glyph floating in
		      the corner, carrying `aria-hidden="true"` ON THE INTERACTIVE ELEMENT, which removes a
		      working control from the accessibility tree entirely. No bio-authoring control exists
		      to lose: v2's Bio tab never authored anything, and D5 forbids this shell emitting a
		      `data-action` its v2 counterpart lacks. --}}
		<button type="button" class="v3-add" data-origin="feature" data-action="itemCreate">
			<i class="fa-solid fa-square-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
			<span>{{localize "wod.labels.add.item"}}</span>
		</button>
	</div>

	<div class="v3-tabbody">
		<div class="v3-tabmain">

			{{!-- ── IDENTITY (formerly the standalone Bio tab) ──────────────────────────────────
			      Reproduced verbatim from `v3/bio.hbs` — see this file's header for why nothing here
			      is a fresh design decision. --}}
			<div class="v3-section v3-bioidentity">

				{{!-- THE PORTRAIT IS A MODULE INTEGRATION POINT, not just an image. `class="profile-img"`
				      plus `data-edit="img"` is the pair image-replacement modules key on — Tokenizer
				      and its relatives look for exactly that, and it is what makes the portrait
				      behave the same here as in every other system.

				      It used to be emitted ONLY on the unlocked, permitted branch, so for most of a
				      session — sheet locked, just being read — no module could see the portrait at
				      all. The two are now separated, because they answer different questions:
				        `data-edit="img"`      MAY this image be replaced -> permission, not lock state
				        `data-action="editImage"`  does OUR click open the picker -> unlocked only
				      A user without `changeActorImage` gets neither, so nothing advertises an edit
				      hook to someone who cannot use it.

				      Right-click to show the image to the table is bound separately, in
				      `PCActorSheetV3.#bindPortraitShare` — on the CONTEXT menu precisely so that the
				      left-click contract above stays untouched. --}}
				<div class="v3-portrait">
					{{#if userpermissions.changeActorImage}}
						<img class="profile-img {{#if (eq actor.img 'icons/svg/mystery-man.svg')}}defaultimage{{/if}}{{#unless locked}} pointer{{/unless}}"
							src="{{actor.img}}" title="{{actor.name}}" alt="{{actor.name}}"
							data-edit="img"{{#unless locked}} data-action="editImage"{{/unless}} />
					{{else}}
						<img class="profile-img {{#if (eq actor.img 'icons/svg/mystery-man.svg')}}defaultimage{{/if}}" src="{{actor.img}}" alt="{{actor.name}}" />
					{{/if}}
				</div>

				<div class="v3-biocore">
					<div class="v3-fields">
						<label class="v3-field">
							<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.name'}}</span>
							{{#if locked}}
								<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.name}}" autocomplete="off" readonly aria-readonly="true" />
							{{else}}
								<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="name" type="text" value="{{actor.name}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
							{{/if}}
						</label>

						{{#if (ne actor.system.settings.splat config.splat.changeling)}}
							{{#if (ne (checkSystemsetting "viewBiotabPermission") "mini")}}
								<label class="v3-field">
									<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.nature'}}</span>
									{{#if locked}}
										<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.nature}}" autocomplete="off" readonly aria-readonly="true" />
									{{else}}
										<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.bio.nature" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.nature}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
									{{/if}}
								</label>
							{{/if}}

							<label class="v3-field">
								<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.demeanor'}}</span>
								{{#if locked}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.demeanor}}" autocomplete="off" readonly aria-readonly="true" />
								{{else}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.bio.demeanor" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.demeanor}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
								{{/if}}
							</label>
						{{/if}}

						{{#if (ne (checkSystemsetting "viewBiotabPermission") "mini")}}
							<label class="v3-field">
								<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.concept'}}</span>
								{{#if locked}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.concept}}" autocomplete="off" readonly aria-readonly="true" />
								{{else}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.bio.concept" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.concept}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
								{{/if}}
							</label>

							<label class="v3-field">
								<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.derangement'}}</span>
								{{#if locked}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.derangement}}" autocomplete="off" readonly aria-readonly="true" />
								{{else}}
									<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.bio.derangement" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.derangement}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
								{{/if}}
							</label>
						{{/if}}
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="v3-biosplat">
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/bio_splatfields.hbs" locked=locked}}
				</div>

			</div>

			{{!-- The splatfield prose. CLAMP_AT = 600, measured on the stored HTML string. See
			      `v3/bio.hbs`'s header for the full reasoning behind disclosure-not-clamp.

			      link-mage-focus-as-items — `paradigm`/`practice`/`instruments` are excluded from
			      THIS loop for a mage ONLY (the `eqAny` test below), and ONLY here: `context.splatfields`
			      itself is left untouched, because it is the exact object `bio_splatfields.hbs` also
			      reads and that partial is SHARED with the v2 sheet's `bio.hbs` — mutating the object
			      would blank these three boxes on v2 too, which is explicitly out of scope. A wraith's
			      four textbox fields (`life`/`death`/`regret`/`thorns`) are unaffected: none of their
			      keys match, and the `eq splat mage` half of the test is false for every wraith anyway. --}}
			{{#each splatfields as |field key|}}
				{{#if (eq field.type "textbox")}}
					{{#unless (and (eq actor.system.settings.splat config.splat.mage) (eqAny key "paradigm" "practice" "instruments"))}}
						<div class="v3-section">
							{{#if ../locked}}
								{{#if (gt field.value.length 600)}}
									<details class="v3-prose">
										<summary class="v3-prosesummary">
											<i class="fa-solid fa-angles-right v3-prosechevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
											<span class="v3-proselabel splatFont">{{localize field.label}}</span>
										</summary>
										<div class="v3-prosebody">
											{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline=field.label locked=../locked headline=false prosename=(concat "system.bio.splatfields." key ".value") prosevalue=field.value proseenriched=field.enriched}}
										</div>
									</details>
								{{else}}
									{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline=field.label locked=../locked headline=false prosename=(concat "system.bio.splatfields." key ".value") prosevalue=field.value proseenriched=field.enriched}}
								{{/if}}
							{{else}}
								{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline=field.label locked=../locked headline=false prosename=(concat "system.bio.splatfields." key ".value") prosevalue=field.value proseenriched=field.enriched}}
							{{/if}}
						</div>
					{{/unless}}
				{{/if}}
			{{/each}}

			{{!-- link-mage-focus-as-items — the three textbox boxes excluded above, replaced with three
			      labelled blocks of Focus Item rows (design D2: rendered here, where Focus already
			      lived — this is where the standalone Bio tab's splatfield prose merged to, §8.1/§8.2;
			      D3: `focus_item.hbs`, not `feature_item.hbs` — see that partial's own header for why.
			      A follow-up after the initial ship made each row's eye icon open the item's own
			      `ItemViewer` window, the same gesture every other row on this sheet uses — see
			      `focus_item.hbs`'s header for the mechanism it reuses).

			      Always three headings, mirroring the three boxes they replace: a mage with zero
			      Instruments still had an (empty) Instruments box before this change, and a heading
			      that disappears when a category happens to be empty would read as "this mage has no
			      Instruments field" rather than "no Instruments picked yet".

			      `mageFocusParadigms`/`mageFocusPractices`/`mageFocusInstruments` are built by THIS
			      part's own preparer chain (`prepareFeatureContext` -> `addBioContext`,
			      pc-actor-sheet.js) for every actor, mage or not — see that function's own comment for
			      why an unconditional build is the safer default in this sheet. --}}
			{{#if (eq actor.system.settings.splat config.splat.mage)}}
				{{!-- add-prism-of-focus-foundry — task 1.3: the structured section REPLACES the
				      free-text-replacement Paradigm/Practice Focus-item lists when `hasprismoffocus`
				      is active (they are the same underlying `wod.types.paradigm`/`wod.types.practice`
				      Feature items link-mage-focus-as-items already reads, so both simply wouldn't
				      show independent facts once a rated Práctica exists). Instrumentos is explicitly
				      NOT touched (A25/C2 Non-goal) — that block always renders, prism or not. --}}
				{{#unless prismActive}}
					<div class="v3-section v3-focusblock">
						<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize 'wod.spheres.paradigm'}}</h3>
						{{#if mageFocusParadigms.length}}
							<div class="v3-focuslist">
								{{#each mageFocusParadigms as |item|}}
									{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/focus_item.hbs" item=item}}
								{{/each}}
							</div>
						{{else}}
							<p class="information-area">{{localize 'wod.labels.none'}}</p>
						{{/if}}
					</div>

					<div class="v3-section v3-focusblock">
						<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize 'wod.spheres.practice'}}</h3>
						{{#if mageFocusPractices.length}}
							<div class="v3-focuslist">
								{{#each mageFocusPractices as |item|}}
									{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/focus_item.hbs" item=item}}
								{{/each}}
							</div>
						{{else}}
							<p class="information-area">{{localize 'wod.labels.none'}}</p>
						{{/if}}
					</div>
				{{else}}
					<div class="v3-section v3-focusblock">
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/mage/prism_tenets.hbs"}}
					</div>
					<div class="v3-section v3-focusblock">
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/mage/prism_practices.hbs"}}
					</div>
					<div class="v3-section v3-focusblock">
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/mage/prism_practice_traits.hbs"}}
					</div>
				{{/unless}}

				<div class="v3-section v3-focusblock">
					<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize 'wod.spheres.instruments'}}</h3>
					{{#if mageFocusInstruments.length}}
						<div class="v3-focuslist">
							{{#each mageFocusInstruments as |item|}}
								{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/focus_item.hbs" item=item}}
							{{/each}}
						</div>
					{{else}}
						<p class="information-area">{{localize 'wod.labels.none'}}</p>
					{{/if}}
				</div>

				{{!-- reorganize-mage-sheet-v3 D4 — Resonancia y Sinergia used to render here, always,
				      for splat mage (add-mage-resonance's original placement). It moved to the Stats
				      tab instead, directly under Fuerza de Voluntad in the Areté/Willpower column
				      (`stats_advantages.hbs`), so it renders exactly once on the sheet instead of
				      here AND as a `simpledots` Poderes section. `context.resonanceMarks` is built
				      by `addResonanceContext`, called from `prepareStatContext` now, not from this
				      tab's preparer — nothing here reads that key any more. --}}
			{{/if}}

			{{#if graphicsettings.useLinkPlatform}}
				<div class="v3-section">
					<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize 'wod.bio.worldanvil'}}</h3>

					{{#if locked}}
						<p class="v3-linkline">
							{{#if (ne actor.system.bio.worldanvil "")}}
								<a href="{{actor.system.bio.worldanvil}}" target="_blank">{{localize 'wod.bio.worldanvillink'}}</a>
							{{else}}
								{{localize 'wod.bio.noworldanvillink'}}
							{{/if}}
						</p>
					{{else}}
						<div class="v3-fields">
							<label class="v3-field">
								<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize 'wod.bio.worldanvil'}}</span>
								<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.bio.worldanvil" type="text" value="{{actor.system.bio.worldanvil}}" data-dtype="String" autocomplete="off" />
							</label>
						</div>
					{{/if}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			<div class="v3-section">
				{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline="wod.bio.appearance" locked=locked headline=false prosename="system.bio.appearance" prosevalue=appearance proseenriched=enrichedAppearance}}
			</div>

			{{#if (ne (checkSystemsetting "viewBiotabPermission") "mini")}}
				<div class="v3-section">
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline="wod.bio.background" locked=locked headline=false prosename="system.bio.background" prosevalue=background proseenriched=enrichedBackground}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{#if isGM}}
				<div class="v3-section">
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline="wod.bio.tips" locked=locked headline=false prosename="system.bio.roleplaytip" prosevalue=roleplaytip proseenriched=enrichedRoleplaytip}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- ── FEATURES (the original content of this tab) ────────────────────────────────── --}}
			<div class="v3-section">

				{{!-- Blood Bond, Boon and Oath render for EVERY splat on `length > 0`, and that is
				      deliberate: the CREATE buttons are gated per line, the render is not, because hiding
				      an item that exists also hides the delete button that is the only way to remove it. --}}
				{{#if (gt bloodbounds.length 0)}}
					<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
						{{#each bloodbounds as |item id|}}
							{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.bloodbound" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.bloodbound" showtype=true}}
						{{/each}}
					</div>
				{{/if}}

				{{#if (gt boons.length 0)}}
					<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
						{{#each boons as |item id|}}
							{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.boon" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.boon" showtype=true}}
						{{/each}}
					</div>
				{{/if}}

				{{#if (gt oaths.length 0)}}
					<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
						{{#each oaths as |item id|}}
							{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.oath" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.oath" showtype=true}}
						{{/each}}
					</div>
				{{/if}}

				{{!-- Passions and Fetters — the wraith's own rated Feature kinds. Dark Passions are NOT
				      here: `add-wraith-shadow-budget §2.2` moved them into `feature_shadow.hbs` precisely
				      so they cannot sit in the next row of the same list as the Passions and be read as
				      one pool. Both pass `valuefirst`, like the Backgrounds block used to, and for the
				      same reason. --}}
				{{#if (gt passions.length 0)}}
					<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
						{{#each passions as |item id|}}
							{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.passion" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.passion" showtype=true valuefirst=item.system.value}}
						{{/each}}
					</div>
				{{/if}}

				{{#if (gt fetters.length 0)}}
					<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
						{{#each fetters as |item id|}}
							{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs" actor=../actor item=item locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.fetter" deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.fetter" showtype=true valuefirst=item.system.value}}
						{{/each}}
					</div>
				{{/if}}

				{{!-- The relationship roster: ONE sub-kind (`wod.types.connection`) grouped by
				      `system.relation`, with each group's name and dots taken from the actor's own
				      Background item. The reasoning is at `parts/feature.hbs:184-223`; what matters here
				      is that the ENTRY is authored inline in both files because no partial exists for it.

				      The portrait is NOT a picker and carries no `data-edit`, so it gets no `pointer`
				      class — clicking it does nothing, and the sheet must not offer a hand cursor that
				      says otherwise. The description is triple-stashed because it is already-enriched
				      HTML off the sheet context. --}}
				{{#if hasConnections}}
					{{#each connections as |group|}}
						<div class="headlineGroup splatFont">
							{{group.label}}
							{{#if group.rating}}{{#numLoop group.rating}}&#9679;{{/numLoop}}{{/if}}
							({{group.count}})
						</div>

						<div class="feature-itemlistarea">
							{{#each group.entries as |item id|}}
								<div class="sheet-boxcontainer connection-entry">

									<div class="shape-panel-image connection-portrait">
										<img class="profile-img shape-image{{#unless item.hasPortrait}} shape-image-empty{{/unless}}"
										     src="{{item.portraitSrc}}" title="{{item.name}}" alt="{{item.name}}" />
									</div>

									<div class="connection-body">

										{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_item.hbs"
											actor=../../actor item=item locked=../../locked
											edittitle="wod.labels.edit.connection"
											deletetitle="wod.labels.remove.connection"
											showtype=false}}

										{{#if item.hasDescription}}
											<div class="connection-description">{{{item.enrichedDescription}}}</div>
										{{/if}}

										{{#if (ne item.system.link "")}}
											<a class="connection-link" href="{{item.system.link}}" target="_blank">{{localize 'wod.connections.link'}}</a>
										{{else}}
											<span class="information-area connection-link">{{localize 'wod.connections.nolink'}}</span>
										{{/if}}

									</div>

								</div>
							{{/each}}
						</div>
					{{/each}}
				{{/if}}

				{{!-- add-pc-sheet-v3 §8.5 — Backgrounds/Merits/Flaws/Other Traits are NOT listed here
				      any more; they render once, on the Stats tab, which is the only place their
				      rating is editable. See this file's header for the measured reason. So the
				      empty-state gate below no longer tests their length: from THIS tab's own point
				      of view they are no longer content it owns. --}}
				{{#if (and (not bloodbounds.length) (not boons.length) (not oaths.length) (not passions.length) (not fetters.length) (not hasConnections))}}
					<p class="v3-empty">{{localize "wod.notes.empty"}}</p>
				{{/if}}

			</div>

			{{!-- The Shadow's own area — Archetype, Angst, Dark Passions and Thorns, with the Shadow's
			      10-point pool named and the Dark-Passion ceiling shown. It gates itself on
			      `hasshadowarea`, so it renders for a wraith (including empty, which is the normal state
			      of a freshly imported one) and for nobody else. Untouched. --}}
			{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/feature_shadow.hbs"}}

			{{!-- ── THE EXPERIENCE LEDGERS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
			      Read the DOM-contract section this file inherited from the pre-merge version before
			      changing the nesting below. The toggle must stay exactly three elements deep inside
			      `.v3-xphead`, `.v3-xphead` must stay a SIBLING of the ledger, and the ledger must keep
			      the literal `addexp`/`spentexp` class its toggle's `data-type` names, plus `hide`.

			          `ItemHelper._onTableCollapse`  : `et.parent().parent().parent().siblings('.' + dataset.type)`
			          `_restoreUnfoldState`          : `ele.parentElement.parentElement.parentElement`, then
			                                           siblings filtered by `classList.contains(type)`,
			                                           only for buttons whose `data-sheet` equals
			                                           `CONFIG.worldofdarkness.sheettype.mortal`
			                                           (pc-actor-sheet.js:545-581)

			      The toggle stays an `<i>` rather than a `<button>` for the reason recorded in the
			      pre-merge version of this file: `_onTableCollapse` swaps the Font Awesome class on
			      `event.currentTarget` itself, so it cannot move to a child the way every other v3
			      button's glyph does, and `.wod20 button:not(.header-control)` sets `font-family` at a
			      specificity that out-ranks `.fa-solid` and paints a tofu box on a bare `<button>`. --}}
			<div class="v3-section v3-xpgrid">

				<div class="v3-xpcol">
					<div class="v3-xphead">
						<div class="v3-xpheadrow">
							<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.labels.notes.expearned"}}</h3>
							<span class="v3-xptotal">{{getTotalExperience actor "earned"}}</span>
							<div class="v3-xptoggle">
								<i class="icon unfold button pointer fa-solid fa-angles-right"
									title="{{localize 'wod.labels.show.experience'}}"
									data-sheet="{{config.sheettype.mortal}}" data-type="addexp"></i>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="hide addexp v3-xpledger" data-area="addexp">
						{{#if (getEarnedExperience actor)}}
							<table class="v3-table v3-xptable">
								<caption class="v3-sr-only">{{localize "wod.labels.notes.expearned"}}</caption>
								<thead>
									<tr>
										<th scope="col">{{localize "wod.labels.description"}}</th>
										<th scope="col" class="v3-num">{{localize "wod.experience.experience"}}</th>
										<th scope="col" class="v3-actioncol"></th>
									</tr>
								</thead>
								<tbody>
									{{#each (getEarnedExperience actor) as |item id|}}
										<tr>
											<td>
												{{#if (ne item.system.description "")}}
													{{item.system.description}}
												{{else}}
													{{localize "wod.notes.descriptionmissing"}}
												{{/if}}
											</td>
											<td class="v3-num">{{item.system.amount}}</td>
											<td class="v3-rowactions">
												{{#if (eq ../locked false)}}
													<a class="item-edit" title="{{localize 'wod.labels.edit.experience'}}" data-type="Experience" data-itemid="{{item.id}}" data-action="itemEdit"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i></a>
													<a class="item-delete" title="{{localize 'wod.labels.remove.experience'}}" data-type="Experience" data-itemid="{{item.id}}" data-action="itemDelete"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-trash-can"></i></a>
												{{/if}}
											</td>
										</tr>
									{{/each}}
								</tbody>
							</table>
						{{/if}}
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="v3-xpcol">
					<div class="v3-xphead">
						<div class="v3-xpheadrow">
							<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.labels.notes.expspend"}}</h3>
							<span class="v3-xptotal">{{getTotalExperience actor "spent"}}</span>
							<div class="v3-xptoggle">
								<i class="icon unfold button pointer fa-solid fa-angles-right"
									title="{{localize 'wod.labels.show.spentexp'}}"
									data-sheet="{{config.sheettype.mortal}}" data-type="spentexp"></i>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="hide spentexp v3-xpledger" data-area="spentexp">
						{{#if (getSpendExperience actor)}}
							<table class="v3-table v3-xptable">
								<caption class="v3-sr-only">{{localize "wod.labels.notes.expspend"}}</caption>
								<thead>
									<tr>
										<th scope="col">{{localize "wod.labels.description"}}</th>
										<th scope="col" class="v3-num">{{localize "wod.experience.experience"}}</th>
										<th scope="col" class="v3-actioncol"></th>
									</tr>
								</thead>
								<tbody>
									{{#each (getSpendExperience actor) as |item id|}}
										<tr>
											<td>
												{{#if (ne item.system.description "")}}
													{{item.system.description}}
												{{else}}
													{{localize "wod.notes.descriptionmissing"}}
												{{/if}}
											</td>
											<td class="v3-num">
												{{#if item.system.isspent}}
													{{item.system.amount}}
												{{else}}
													{{localize "wod.notes.unspent"}}
												{{/if}}
											</td>
											<td class="v3-rowactions">
												{{#if (eq ../locked false)}}
													<a class="item-edit" title="{{localize 'wod.labels.edit.experience'}}" data-type="Experience" data-itemid="{{item.id}}" data-action="itemEdit"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i></a>
													<a class="item-delete" title="{{localize 'wod.labels.remove.experience'}}" data-type="Experience" data-itemid="{{item.id}}" data-action="itemDelete"><i class="icon fa-solid fa-trash-can"></i></a>
												{{/if}}
											</td>
										</tr>
									{{/each}}
								</tbody>
							</table>
						{{/if}}
					</div>
				</div>

			</div>

		</div>

		<aside class="v3-macrorail">
			{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/macro_icons.hbs"}}
		</aside>
	</div>

</section>
